 "schema": 1,
 "milestone": "M2b",
 "_comment": [
  "libOPNMIDI (YM2612 OPN2 / YM2608 OPNA) bank list. Every bank with enabled:true AND an image_path becomes two variants in variants.json: opn-<slug> (--emu-nuked-3438) and opn-<slug>-opna (--emu-mame-opna). Hand-edited; re-run python3 -m catalog.variants after changes.",
  "M2b decision (2026-08-21): the 7 distinct fm_banks/*.wopn shipped in the pinned libOPNMIDI commit are installed in the image at /opt/banks/wopn/<slug>.wopn with their readme files and are enabled - including the three without a licence statement (gems-fmlib-gmize, nineko, tomsoft), which get a legal_note and a row in review.md (same treatment as the libADLMIDI embedded banks, issue #301). Set enabled:false (or publish:false) here to withdraw one.",
  "OPN2BankEditor-only files (ed-xg, tomsoft-orig, ed-gems-fmlib-gmize, ed-gm-old) are NOT in the image (licence review pending; render/banks/README.md explains how to add a bank with a licence file) and stay enabled:false; gm, ed-tomsoft and ed-gm are byte-identical duplicates of shipped banks.",
  "Per-bank optional keys read by variants.py: publish (default true), completeness (default full_gm), bank_map (default gm), quality (list), publish_note (appended to legal_note).",
  "OPN2BankEditor's Bank_Examples/ also holds GEMS .bnk, GYB, Mucom88, BambooTracker and Y12 instrument sets that are not WOPN files; opnmidiplay loads WOPN only, so they would need conversion in the editor first (not planned).",
  "Render template (verified M2b, WAVE_ONLY build): cd <tmp> && ln -s /songs/<id>.mid <id>.mid && opnmidiplay -f32 -vm 0 --gain 2.0 --chips 2 --emu-nuked-3438 /opt/banks/wopn/<slug>.wopn <id>.mid  -> <id>.mid.wav (44100 Hz). Options first, then the bank (positional, no -b), then the MIDI."
 ],
